  "contentYjsBase64": "",
  "contentPlaintext": "<bold>📖 Academic Workspace Guide</bold>\nWelcome to your central hub for your Senior Project. This workspace is engineered to streamline collaboration between student team members, project leads, teaching assistants, and your supervisor.\n<bold>1. Workspace Ecosystem & Roles</bold>\nThis environment utilizes strict academic role permissions to maintain evaluation integrity.\nRole\nWorkspace Label\nPrimary Responsibilities\nPermissions\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">OWNER</textStyle></bold>\nSupervisor\nAcademic oversight, grading, milestone approvals.\nFull Access / Final Sign-off\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">ADMIN</textStyle></bold>\nTeaching Assistant\nTechnical mentorship, initial code reviews, grading support.\nFull Access minus deletion\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">MANAGER</textStyle></bold>\nProject Lead\nTask assignment, timeline management, submission initiation.\nManage Tasks & Drafts\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">MEMBER</textStyle></bold>\nStudent\nExecution of research, design, coding, and internal testing.\nEdit Drafts / Complete Tasks\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">VIEWER</textStyle></bold>\nExternal Reviewer\nCross-examination, feedback, and independent grading.\nRead-Only + Commenting\n<bold>2. Directory & Folder Architecture</bold>\nThe workspace is structured into specific folders. Do not alter the root file structure without supervisor permission:\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">📋 Administration</textStyle></bold>: Governance documents, team contracts, and communication frameworks.\n<italic>📂 Meeting Minutes</italic>: Historical logs of weekly syncs and formal supervisor reviews.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">📝 Requirements</textStyle></bold>: Problem definitions, scoping, and external source analysis.\n<italic>📂 Research & Resources</italic>: Academic papers, competitive benchmarks, and literature references.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">🏗️ Design</textStyle></bold>: Visual diagrams, behavioral models, architectural maps, and data schemas.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">💻 Implementation</textStyle></bold>: Technical notes, deployment pipelines, configuration guides, and API documentation.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">🧪 Testing</textStyle></bold>: Quality assurance protocols, test plans, automation metrics, and validation logs.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">📊 Reports</textStyle></bold>: Recurring status logs and the final comprehensive capstone thesis.\n<bold>3. The Academic Submission Workflow</bold>\nFor milestones requiring formal review (marked with a submission toggle in your dashboard), you must follow the strict submission workflow system.\n[ Draft Mode ] ➔ [ Lead Reviews ] ➔ [ Submitted ] ➔ [ Supervisor Action ]\n       │                                                     │\n       │                                      ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐\n       ▼                                      ▼                             ▼\n(Student Edits)                       [ Approved / Locked ]       [ Revision Required ]\n<bold>Step 1: Draft Creation (Students)</bold>\nWork collaboratively within the designated template.\nKeep the document tag as <code>[DRAFT]</code> in the title until complete.\n<bold>Step 2: Internal Verification (Project Lead)</bold>\nThe Project Lead runs a quality check against the faculty evaluation rubric.\nThe Lead triggers the formal <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">\"Submit for Review\"</textStyle></bold> action via the workspace portal.\n<bold>Step 3: Evaluation Phase (Supervisor & Reviewers)</bold>\nThe document instantly transitions to <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Read-Only</textStyle></bold> for students.\nSupervisors and External Reviewers append contextual inline comments directly to the text.\n<bold>Step 4: Final Outcome</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Approved</textStyle></bold>: The document is digitally locked. It serves as a historical milestone archive.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Revision Required</textStyle></bold>: The document unlocks for student editing. A clear revision deadline is set via the task board.\n<bold>4. Task Management and Metadata Tags</bold>\nEvery task created on the team board must map to one of these standardized functional taxonomy tags:\n💜 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">deliverable</textStyle></bold>: Items bound to a formal grade or project milestone.\n💙 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">research</textStyle></bold>: Exploratory study, literature parsing, or experimental benchmarking.\n💚 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">implementation</textStyle></bold>: Code architecture, component builds, and hardware layout.\n💛 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">meeting</textStyle></bold>: Administrative sync ups, agendas, and presentation preparation.\n❤️ <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">review</textStyle></bold>: Work blocks halted explicitly awaiting internal peer or supervisor sign-off.\n🖤 <bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">blocked</textStyle></bold>: Task halted by external dependencies (e.g., missing API access, hardware shipment).\n<bold>5. Ground Rules for Success</bold>\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Commit Often, Log Daily</textStyle></bold>: Ensure your implementation notes folder updates dynamically as your codebase evolves.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">No Ghost Meetings</textStyle></bold>: Every formal sync with your supervisor must have an entry in <code>Meeting Minutes</code> within 12 hours of completion.\n<bold><textStyle color=\"\" fontFamily=\"\" fontSize=\"null\">Respect the Lock</textStyle></bold>: Do not attempt to duplicate or bypass documents locked by the submission system. Use tracking branches for code changes.",
